__pycache__/
*.pyc
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/

# Secrets and runtime state — never committed. The repo carries declarative
# configuration only; see runtime/ for the sanitized, restorable form.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# The vault seed's `.env` is not a credential file — it is how the obsidian-wiki
# tools resolve vault path, categories and page limits, and the deploy installs
# it into the runtime vault. Named `.env` by that convention, so the rule above
# shadows it; committed deliberately. Secrets live in ~/.hermes/.env.
!runtime/vault-seed/.env
*.token
*.secret
auth.json
auth.lock
*.db
*.db-*
logs/
sessions/
request_dump_*.json
runtime-state/
.hermes/
channel_directory.json

# Wiki vault: raw Hostex conversations are staging only, never committed —
# they are verbatim guest messages, and regenerable from the API besides.
# Any path, not just ./vault: `--vault` accepts a location, so an in-repo vault
# elsewhere would otherwise be tracked. runtime/vault-seed/.env points OBSIDIAN_RAW_DIR
# here (installed to vault/.env in the runtime vault at deploy time).
**/_raw/

# Scratch vault the on-demand end-to-end run creates. It holds a full copy of
# the verbatim conversations, so it is ignored for the same reason _raw/ is.
.e2e-vault/

# knightwatch materializes declared review siblings here during a review.
.siblings/
